# scene -> motion text (what moves). Used by batch.sh
motion_tearoom="steam curls up from the teapot and the two cups; the sheer curtains sway softly in a light breeze; leaves outside the window rustle; the flowers in the glass jar nod slightly; the pendulum clock ticks; light shifts gently across the table. Everything else perfectly still."
motion_livingroom="the fire flickers and crackles with rising wisps of smoke; the sleeping cat breathes slowly and its tail twitches once; steam rises from the mug on the coffee table; the sheer curtains sway in a light breeze; leaves outside the window rustle; dappled light shifts on the wall; the lantern glows softly. Everything else perfectly still."
motion_bedroom="the sheer curtains billow softly in a light breeze; leaves and hills outside the window sway gently; dappled light drifts slowly across the bed and wall; steam rises from the cup on the bedside table; the lamp glows with a faint flicker. Everything else perfectly still."
motion_greenhouse="gentle rain droplets run slowly down the glass panes; leaves, ferns and orchid blooms sway slightly; the hanging basket sways; a soft breeze through the open door moves the garden outside; light and mist shift softly. Everything else perfectly still."
motion_sunset="the young woman and the golden retriever sit still from behind: her braid and shawl stir in the breeze, she breathes softly, the dog's ears flick and it breathes; steam rises from the teapot; tall grasses and wildflowers sway; clouds drift very slowly; the string lights glow; smoke from the cottage chimney rises. Everything else perfectly still."
light_day="calm bright daytime"
light_dusk="golden dusk, warm low sun, long soft shadows"
light_night="quiet night, deep blue tones with warm lamp and window glow"
